<title>FINLAND: Nokia says seals A$200 mln network deal.</title>
<headline>Nokia says seals A$200 mln network deal.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish telecommunications group Nokia Oy said on Wednesday it had won a A$200 million order for a mobile phone network expansion from Australian Optus Communications.</p>
<p>&quot;The frame agreement, which covers the period 1997 to 1999, means Nokia will continue as the sole supplier to Optus of GSM (Global System for Mobile Communication) base station subsystems,&quot; Nokia said in a statement.</p>
</text>
